# 1v1, cloud locks to the PC (BENCH-253), round 7: every per-robot line that locked on the cloud (95% low end above 0,
# live turn time; coverage/shards/locks.tsv, coverage/shards/round7-draft.md) after round 6 (PR #890) ran, locked on 12 fresh PC seeds:
#   rf (RAM-15 ram-flee, off on master until this card holds it): Miedzix +3.0 (low +1.9), Kuramatron +2.3 (+1.4, 24 seeds),
#      Gajeel +1.9 (+1.1), DOSexe +2.5 (+1.4), Scrapple +1.5 (+0.8), Caligula +3.0 (+1.4, 24), SabreuseNano +1.7 (+0.6, 24),
#      SuperRamFire +5.0 (+2.0), Detektor3 +2.6 (+1.6), Bulldozer +1.9 (+0.9, 24), Lifestealer +2.0 (+0.9, 36), Roberto +1.6 (+0.9),
#      RamboT +1.6 (+0.9, 24), xbots +4.1 (+0.8), WallGuy3 +0.9 (+0.3, 36), Chaser +2.1 (+1.6), SCALPBot +2.1 (+0.9),
#      Trinity +1.7 (+1.0), JGAP130166 +1.7 (+1.0), SledgeHammer +2.2 (+0.9), DizzyA +1.2 (+0.8, 24), URDOS +2.3 (+1.1, 24),
#      Hodur +2.5 (+1.5, 24), FollowFire +1.7 (+0.9, 24), Squaraus +1.3 (+0.5), Eagle +1.2 (+0.6, 24); 12 seeds unless marked
#   sp2 (DODGE-6 shot-dodge planner): ArthurPanzergon +3.9 (+2.4), Tn1 +1.8 (+1.1, 24 seeds), Rookie +2.6 (+1.7), NanoR2 +2.6 (+1.6)
#   rwl (MOVE-46 ram wait on a disabled enemy): Calypso +1.1 (+0.2, 48 seeds)
#   Each gain is the smaller of the reads against c and against an A/A twin. WallGuy3 and Calypso only just clear 0; the PC decides them.
#   livematch  the released jar and BeepBoop 2.0 on the 31-robot panel at the live constant, read against live
#   lock       the 31 robots  c / aa / rf / sp2 / rwl (each lever arm built with only its own robots)   12 fresh seeds
#              from 43700, --cpu-constant live, in work/pc-locks7 (earlier rounds' battles stay in work/pc-locks to -locks6)
#   gate       each robot judged on its own arm only (lock_prep.py --restrict); it keeps its line where the 95% low end
#              is above 0 (mode_table.py --margin 0)
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-locks --fresh        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-locks --fresh)
#   --fresh because round 6 left this plan's queue state marked complete; an interrupted round 7 resumes without it.
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, 16 workers, truth log off. 1860 lock battles (31 robots, 5 arms, 12 seeds), about 25 minutes
# with the live-match check.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - Per-opponent tailoring: every line names one robot; every other robot, team and melee play bit for bit as master.
#   - Diagnosis first (truth logs against BeepBoop 2.0 and Saguaro 1.1.4):
#     rf: these robots charge at 2-5 px a tick, under RAM-1's 6, so RAM-2 never confirms them and we stay in contact; BeepBoop
#     backs away at 5 px a tick or more (Miedzix: ram damage taken 68 -> 8 a battle with the flee). Shards M, A, C, D, G and the
#     danger box screened the robots that ram us; only locks are here (coverage/shards/move/ramflee/README.md).
#     sp2: non-rammers fought beyond 300 px whose simple or partial aims hit us 2-5x more than BeepBoop does (ArthurPanzergon
#     13.7% vs 2.5%, Tn1 4.0% vs 1.9%); the planner steps off the aimed line (coverage/shards/rereadL, rereadL2; C re-read lane).
#     rwl: Calypso keeps hitting us after we disable it; waiting out the disabled enemy instead of closing held over 48 cloud seeds.
#   - Every robot passed the cloud lock bar first; round 6 held 23 of 44 (#890, banked #896).
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): the watcher's A/A rule needs 10 robots read in both c and aa, which this 31-robot
# lock reaches only near its end (shuffled jobs), so no aa stop rule is set; aa is read in the gate (multiarm.py prints aa against c). The card halts on 30 failed
# battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 60+ skipped turns a battle over the last 24, or no battle in 30 minutes. The
# live-match step stops the card if the PC no longer scores us and BeepBoop as live does (tools/live_match.py exit 3).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on any stop.
# Bank: the owning cloud thread adds the gate's lines on this card's results PR. Nothing is released by the card.
set V = 3.23
set P = --parallel 16 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant live --child-heap 2G
set W = work/pc-locks7
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && (cd .. && mvn -q -DskipTests package) && cp ../hadur-robot/target/hadur117.Hadur_${V}.jar bisect/ && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && python3 tools/lock_prep.py plans/locks-pick.tsv panel-locks.txt plans/pc-locks.arms ${W}-prep && bash ${W}-prep/build.sh && for a in rf sp2 rwl; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar || exit 1; done && bash tools/fetch_live_jar.sh && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-r31.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set livematch-bb.txt && test -f opponents/kc.mega.BeepBoop_2.0.jar && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set panel-locks.txt && mvn -q compile

livematch | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-r31.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 21700 --arms plans/livematch.arms --out work/pc-livematch-rel-live --label pc-locks-livematch --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/live_match.py work/pc-livematch-rel-live/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/pc-locks7-livematch.md
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: stall 30m

lock | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set panel-locks.txt --seeds 12 --seed-base 43700 --arms ${W}-prep/lock.arms --out ${W} --label pc-locks --shuffle-jobs
  after: livematch
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 24
  stop: stall 30m

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks7-lock.md && python3 tools/lock_prep.py --restrict ${W}/arms.tsv ${W}-prep ${W}/arms-picked.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --margin 0 --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks7-lock-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks7-lock-pick.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms-picked.tsv --arms rf sp2 rwl --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_pc-locks7-lock-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/pc-locks7-lock-per-robot.tsv
  after: lock

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-locks7-results "1v1 cloud locks, round 7 (31 robots from the field shards) locked on 12 fresh PC seeds" ${OUT}/pc-locks7-livematch.md ${OUT}/*_pc-locks7-*.md ${OUT}/pc-locks7-lock-per-robot.tsv $(find ${OUT} -maxdepth 1 -name 'pc-locks7-lock-pick.tsv' -size +0c)
  after: gate
